  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given sum is\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{3}{12}+\\frac{5}{1^2+2^2}+\\frac{7}{1^2+2^2+3^2}+\\ldots . . \\\\\n& n \\text {th term }=\\mathrm{T}_n \\\\\n& =\\frac{2 n+1}{\\frac{n(n+1)(2 n+1)}{6}}=\\frac{6}{n(n+1)} \\\\\n& \\text { or } \\mathrm{T}_n=6\\left[\\frac{1}{n}-\\frac{1}{n+1}\\right] \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad \\mathrm{S}_n= \\\\\n& \\sum \\mathrm{T}_n=6 \\sum \\frac{1}{n}-6 \\sum \\frac{1}{n+1}=\\frac{6 n}{n}-\\frac{6}{n+1} \\\\\n& =6-\\frac{6}{n+1}=\\frac{6 n}{n+1} \\\\\n& S_{11}=\\frac{6 \\times 11}{11+1}=\\frac{66}{12}=\\frac{33}{6}=\\frac{11}{2} \\\\\n&\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
